  "description": "meme-id: proof_you_can_be_a_fruit_and_a_vegetable; hasOverallIntent: educational; overall-intent-description: The image displays a pile of ripe red tomatoes with the text overlay 'proof you can be a fruit and a vegetable.' This meme uses the visual of tomatoes (a common food item) to illustrate a botanical fact: tomatoes are botanically classified as fruits because they develop from the flower of the plant and contain seeds, yet they are commonly categorized as vegetables in culinary contexts. The intent is educational or humorous, aiming to clarify a common point of confusion in food classification. There is no toxicity, harmful content, or disparaging metaphor present. The meme relies on juxtaposition of the image (tomatoes) with the text to deliver a factual or lighthearted message about taxonomy, not to attack or demean any group.",
